tutor-skills
============

Intellectual debts, stated plainly.

## The knowledge-base pattern

The idea of an agent *compiling* raw sources into a persistent, cross-linked wiki
— rather than re-retrieving them per query — comes from Andrej Karpathy's
llm-wiki Gist:

    https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f

The five-operation shape built on top of it (compile · ingest · query · lint ·
audit), the raw/wiki/outputs directory layout, and the audit/ feedback channel
with its anchor-window addressing come from the `llm-wiki` skill by Lewis Liu
(lylewis@outlook.com).

**This project does not vendor or redistribute that skill.** tutor-skills is an
independent implementation of a different thing — a learning method — and it runs
on top of any markdown wiki, with or without llm-wiki present. What is inherited
is the idea, and the ancestry is recorded here because ideas have authors.

The parts that are this project's own: the depth-level page format and the rule
that an analogy must state where it breaks; the trustworthiness scale computed by
machine from independent sources and typed checks; the tracks/ layer that argues
for its own ordering; the approach exercises and hint ladder; and the two-phase
domain-layer assembly.

## Tooling

Text extraction leans on Tesseract and Poppler when the corpus capability is in
use; both are called as external programs and neither is redistributed here.
